{"id":122836825807068,"type":"album","name":"Here, My Dear","artist":"Marvin Gaye","year":1978,"weight":31,"info":{"cover":"https://ia800302.us.archive.org/19/items/mbid-4c413791-f9de-4259-b971-1bb2f7c678a4/mbid-4c413791-f9de-4259-b971-1bb2f7c678a4-5486950797.jpg","label":"Motown","kind":"Album","tracks":14,"country":"US","aoty":84,"aoty_user":79,"yt":"GZgHRBFAMTQ","links":{"spotify":"https://open.spotify.com/album/0YbHA3w82FSmpyXxdXfuCv","discogs":"https://www.discogs.com/release/3844543","rateyourmusic":"https://rateyourmusic.com/release/album/marvin-gaye/here-my-dear","musicbrainz":"https://musicbrainz.org/release-group/225a6648-d4d2-3b89-986b-6e515e7a94f0","allmusic":"https://www.allmusic.com/album/mw0000112616","aoty":"https://www.albumoftheyear.org/album/17746-marvin-gaye-here-my-dear.php"},"desc":"Pre-dating the voyeuristic tendencies of reality television by 20 years, Here, My Dear is the sound of divorce on record — exposed in all of its tender-nerve glory for the world to consume. During the amazing success of I Want You and his stellar Live at the London Palladium album, Marvin Gaye was served with divorce papers from his then-wife Anna Gordy Gaye (sister of Motown Records founder Berry Gordy). One of the conditions of the settlement was that Gordy Gaye would receive an extensive percentage of royalties as well as a portion of the advance for his next album. .","producers":"Marvin Gaye","engineers":"Art Stewart, Bill Ravencraft, Fred Ross (2), Tony Houston (2) / Jack Andrews","credits":{"design, art direction":["John Kosh"],"engineer":["Art Stewart","Bill Ravencraft","Fred Ross (2)","Tony Houston (2)"],"illustration [cover]":["Michael Bryan (4)"],"mastered by":["Jack Andrews"],"mixed by":["Art Stewart"],"producer, arranged by, written-by":["Marvin Gaye"]}},"artist_ref":{"id":142830390670993,"name":"Marvin Gaye","info":{"img":"https://cdn-images.dzcdn.net/images/artist/149cf44d269d34d3277b97ea1b907366/1000x1000-000000-80-0-0.jpg"}},"labels":[{"id":20875781